<!--
  Occupella's indexable surface, in full.

  The application itself is ONE url. app.occupella.com is a single-page app
  a sign-in wall: every path vercel.json does not exclude returns the same
  index.html, so listing /inbox, /properties and the rest would be listing the
  same document six times under six names. The canonical tag in index.html
  collapses them for a crawler that arrives at one directly.

  The /legal/*.html files are the exception and the reason this file is worth
  having: they are REAL static documents with their own titles and their own
  text, served straight off the filesystem, and they are the only pages on the
  domain a crawler can read without an account.

  DELIBERATELY NO <lastmod>. It is optional, and a date nothing measures is a
  date that is wrong the day after it is written — a crawler told a page
  changed and finding it unchanged learns to discount the field, which is the
  cost of every fabricated freshness stamp in this product. These documents
  change when the policies change, and nothing in the build can observe that.
  Add real dates here the day something generates them from the files.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/legal/terms.html</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/legal/privacy.html</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/legal/sms.html</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/legal/billing.html</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/legal/subprocessors.html</loc>
  </url>
  <url>
    <loc>https://app.occupella.com/legal/accessibility.html</loc>
  </url>
</urlset>
